---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import IndustryPageTemplate from '../../components/IndustryPageTemplate.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Sight Glass for Pharmaceutical Processing';
const metaTitle = 'Sight Glass for Pharmaceutical | Sanitary Sight Glass — SIGHTSPEC';
const kw = 'sight glass for pharmaceutical';
const desc = 'Sanitary sight glasses for pharmaceutical processing: USP Class VI tri-clamp sight glass with a dead-leg-free design, 316L wetted surfaces and an optional heated anti-fog window for CIP/SIP sterile lines and bioreactors.';
const points = [
  'USP Class VI and FDA-compliant wetted materials engineered for sterile liquid, granulate and powder lines',
  'Dead-leg-free sanitary tri-clamp mounting — no crevices, no product hold-up, no bacteria traps',
  'Borosilicate windows to DIN 7080 that hold up to steam, caustic washes and repeated CIP/SIP cycles',
  'Optional heated anti-fog variant keeps the viewing window clear when vapor condensates on the glass',
];
const longtail = [
  'sanitary sight glass pharma',
  'tri clamp sight glass pharmaceutical',
  'USP class VI sight glass',
  'sight glass for CIP SIP',
  'hygienic sight glass 316L',
  'heated sight glass anti fog',
  'sight glass for bioreactor',
  'pharmaceutical sight glass with light',
  'sight glass for WFI lines',
  'sanitary sight glass 1.5 inch',
];
const recommended = [
  { href: '/products/tri-clamp-sight-glasses/', title: 'SG-100 Tri-Clamp Sight Glass', desc: 'Sanitary quick-clamp sight glass, 316L wetted surfaces, USP Class VI, 1/2"–12".' },
  { href: '/products/tri-clamp-sight-glasses/', title: 'SG-100 Heated Anti-Fog Variant', desc: 'Same sanitary body with an integrated heated window for steam and condensate duty.' },
  { href: '/products/sight-flow-indicators/', title: 'SG-200 Sight Flow Indicator', desc: 'Visual flow verification with sanitary tri-clamp or threaded mounting options.' },
];
---

<Layout title={metaTitle} description={desc}>
  <IndustryPageTemplate title={pageTitle} kw={kw} desc={desc} points={points} longtail={longtail} recommended={recommended}>
    <div slot="chapters">
      <section class="bg-white">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">PHARMA CHALLENGES</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Why Sight Glasses Fail in Sterile Processing</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">A sight glass on a bioreactor, WFI loop or CIP/SIP header has one job: show operators exactly what is happening inside the line. In pharmaceutical service, that job comes with a second, harder requirement — the window itself must never become a contamination risk. Three problems dominate pharma sight glass failures: sterility, dead-legs and glass that cannot survive aggressive cleaning cycles.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600"><strong class="text-navy-950">Sterility.</strong> Standard industrial sight glasses use threaded connections, recessed seals and internal crevices. In a sterile line, every crevice is a place where bioburden can survive a cleaning cycle and re-enter the product stream. A sanitary design starts with a tri-clamp connection, 316L stainless wetted surfaces and gaskets made from materials with USP Class VI statements.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600"><strong class="text-navy-950">Dead-legs.</strong> Any pocket where product or cleaning agent can sit stagnant is a dead-leg. Industry design practice (ASME BPE) treats dead-leg volume as a contamination risk, which is why sanitary sight glasses are built flush with the bore — no ledges, no pockets, no product hold-up — so CIP solution and SIP steam reach every wetted surface.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600"><strong class="text-navy-950">Cleaning cycles.</strong> CIP means caustic and acid washes; SIP means live steam at sterilization temperature. The window sees repeated thermal cycling and chemical attack. Borosilicate glass to DIN 7080 is the standard choice because it absorbs thermal shock without cracking and resists the caustic and acid washes used in CIP. Soda-lime glass is only acceptable for low-temperature, mild duty.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-slate-50">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">RECOMMENDED PRODUCT</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">SG-100 Tri-Clamp Sight Glass for Pharmaceutical Lines</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The SG-100 is our flagship sanitary sight glass, built around the requirements of sterile processing: seamless, dead-leg-free construction, electropolished 316L wetted surfaces and USP Class VI compliant materials. It mounts with standard sanitary tri-clamp fittings, so it installs into existing process lines without special tooling and comes apart in seconds for inspection and gasket change-out.</p>
          <div class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
              <thead class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
                <tr>
                  <th class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold">Parameter</th>
                  <th class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold">SG-100 Specification</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
                <tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-bold text-navy-950">Mounting</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600">Sanitary tri-clamp, 1/2"–12" / DN15–DN300</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-bold text-navy-950">Glass</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600">Borosilicate to DIN 7080 (soda lime optional for mild duty)</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-bold text-navy-950">Metal</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600">304 / 316L SS; Hastelloy or Duplex on request</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-bold text-navy-950">Temperature</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600">Up to 572°F (300°C)</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-bold text-navy-950">Pressure</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600">Full vacuum to 230 psi (1.6 MPa)</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-bold text-navy-950">Approvals</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600">USP Class VI / BPE compliant / FDA</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-500">OEM customization is available: custom tube lengths, lighting options, gasket materials and brand marking — see our <a href="/services/oem-odm/" class="font-semibold text-brand-blue hover:underline">OEM/ODM service</a> for the full list.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-white">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">HEATED ANTI-FOG OPTION</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Heated Anti-Fog Sight Glass: Keeping the Window Clear</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Fogging is the most common complaint on pharmaceutical sight glasses. During SIP, or when a warm vessel sits in a cooler room, vapor condenses on the inside of the glass and the window goes opaque exactly when operators need to confirm the process. The SG-100 heated anti-fog variant integrates a heating element sized for the window diameter, keeping the glass surface above the dew point so the view stays clear through steam and condensate duty.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Spec the heated variant when you run frequent SIP cycles, when the vessel sits in a high-humidity area, or when visual verification is part of your batch records. The heating option is factory-fitted and specified together with the window size, ambient temperature and the utility voltage available at the skid — the right heat load is engineered in, not guessed on site.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-slate-50">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">SELECTION GUIDE</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Selection Essentials for Pharmaceutical Sight Glass</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Match the specification to your line and your quality system:</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
            <li><strong class="text-navy-950">Connection:</strong> the tri-clamp size must match the line bore — 1/2" to 12" is available; confirm the clamp standard and gasket profile.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy-950">Wetted finish:</strong> 316L with electropolished finish; state your required Ra if your specification demands it.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy-950">Glass:</strong> borosilicate to DIN 7080 for thermal shock and chemical resistance; soda lime only for low-temperature, non-sterile duty.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy-950">Gaskets:</strong> EPDM, silicone or PTFE with USP Class VI statements; confirm compatibility with your cleaning chemistry and steam exposure.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy-950">Documentation:</strong> material certificates, USP Class VI test statements and batch traceability records are provided with every shipment.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy-950">Extras:</strong> heated anti-fog window, lighting or illumination, and custom tube length for unusual wall thickness.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-white">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-blue">FAQ</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold text-navy-950 sm:text-3xl">Pharmaceutical Sight Glass Questions</h2>
          <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl space-y-4">
            <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-bold text-navy-950">Is the SG-100 suitable for sterile and aseptic lines?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Yes. The SG-100 uses a sanitary tri-clamp mounting, 316L wetted surfaces and a dead-leg-free bore, with gasket options carrying USP Class VI statements. It is designed for CIP/SIP service and is used on sterile liquid, WFI and bioprocess lines.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-bold text-navy-950">What causes fogging on a pharmaceutical sight glass and how is it prevented?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Fogging is condensation: warm vapor inside meets a cooler glass surface. The heated anti-fog variant keeps the glass above the dew point, so the window stays clear during steam and condensate duty. The right heat load depends on window size and ambient temperature — our engineers spec it with you.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-bold text-navy-950">Which gasket materials are available?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">EPDM, silicone and PTFE, all with USP Class VI statements. The right choice depends on your media and cleaning chemistry — silicone is common for steam service, EPDM for many CIP chemistries, and PTFE where chemical resistance dominates.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-bold text-navy-950">Can the sight glass be cleaned in place?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Yes. The flush, dead-leg-free design lets CIP solution and SIP steam reach every wetted surface. Borosilicate glass to DIN 7080 is selected for the thermal cycling that CIP/SIP brings.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-bold text-navy-950">What documentation do you provide?</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Each shipment includes material certificates, USP Class VI test statements and batch traceability records. Additional documentation can be prepared per your quality system.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </IndustryPageTemplate>

  <CtaBand
    title="Need a Sanitary Sight Glass for Your Pharma Line?"
    subtitle="Send your line size, gasket preference and whether you need the heated anti-fog option — get a specification review and quotation within 24 hours."
  />
</Layout>
